# Frontend Services & Routing

## File Roles
*   `views/` — pages registered in `router.js`.
*   `components/` — shared UI; `components/layout/` page shells and `components/common/` shared pieces (see `ui-style-system.mdc`).
*   `services/services.js` — shared axios instance; domain modules in `*Services.js`.
*   `stores/` — Pinia stores (`defineStore` setup syntax), one per concern (`auth.js`). `stores/index.js` creates the single Pinia instance that `main.js` installs.
*   `composables/` — reusable stateful logic (`useRequest`, `useConfirm`, `useRoles`, `useDeleteUser`, …).
*   `models/` — pure domain and display helpers per entity (`models/users.js`: `roleLabel`, `fullName`, `toRolesPayload`, filters). No HTTP, no Vue state.
*   `config/utils.js` — `errorMessage(error, fallback)`. No storage helpers; app state belongs in a store.
*   `utils/` — other pure helpers; no HTTP calls.

## Domain Service Modules
*   One file per domain: `authServices.js`, `userServices.js`, `areaServices.js`, etc.
*   Default-export an object of methods; each method calls `apiClient` and returns the promise.
*   No axios calls inside views or components — always go through `*Services.js`.

## Data Fetching in Views
*   Call services through `useRequest(service.method, { initial, fallback })`, which returns `{ data, loading, error, run }`. `run(...args)` resolves `true`/`false`, ignores stale responses, and sets `error` from the API message (or `fallback`). Do not hand-roll try/catch, loading flags, or error refs.
    ```javascript
    const { data: areas, loading, error, run: getAreas } =
      useRequest(areaServices.getAreas, { initial: [], fallback: "Failed to fetch areas." });
    onMounted(getAreas);
    ```
*   Feed `loading` / `error` to `PageShell` (whole-page loads) or `ListState` (lists).
*   Destructive actions go through `useConfirm()` with `onConfirm` doing the request, so the dialog shows the spinner and API errors. A confirm + request repeated across views becomes its own composable (e.g. `useDeleteUser`).

## Axios Client (`services/services.js`)
*   `baseURL`: `http://localhost:3200/api/` in development; in production it must match `API_PREFIX` in `backend/server.js`.
*   `withCredentials: true`.
*   Request interceptor: attach `Authorization: Bearer <token>` from `useAuthStore().token`.
*   Response interceptor: on `401` or an unauthorized message, `useAuthStore().signOut()` and `router.push({ name: "login" })`.
*   FormData uploads: delete `Content-Type` header so the browser sets the boundary.

## Router Conventions (`router.js`)
*   vue-router 4 with `createWebHistory`.
*   Named routes (`name: "userDetails"`); `props: true` on routes with `:id` params.
*   Lazy-load views with `component: () => import("./views/…")`; only `Login` and `Home` are imported eagerly.
*   Access and navigation are declared on the route's `meta`:
    *   `public: true` — open without a session (login).
    *   `roles: [...]` — the user needs any one (admins always pass); no `roles` = any signed-in user.
    *   `nav: "Label"`, `icon: "mdi-…"` — adds the page to the MenuBar/Sidebar, shown only when `canOpen(route)` is true. Never hand-add nav links.
*   `router.beforeEach` enforces these per `auth-patterns.mdc`.

## Shared State (Pinia)
Share state across components through a Pinia store, not `window` events or prop drilling: components re-render when the store changes. Components call `useXStore()`; code outside components (router guards, axios interceptors) may call it too, because `stores/index.js` makes the app's Pinia active on import. Persist to `localStorage` inside the store when state must survive a reload (see `stores/auth.js`).

## Production Deploy
Copy `public/.htaccess` to `dist/` on build — SPA fallback rewrite and cache headers for hashed assets.
